{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine how many perfect squares are factors of \\(2 \\times 4 \\times 6 \\times 8 \\times 10 \\times 12\\), we start by finding the prime factorization of the product.\n\nFirst, we factorize each of the numbers:\n\\[2 = 2\\]\n\\[4 = 2^2\\]\n\\[6 = 2 \\times 3\\]\n\\[8 = 2^3\\]\n\\[10 = 2 \\times 5\\]\n\\[12 = 2^2 \\times 3\\]\n\nNow, we multiply these factorizations together:\n\\[2 \\times 4 \\times 6 \\times 8 \\times 10 \\times 12 = 2 \\times 2^2 \\times (2 \\times 3) \\times 2^3 \\times (2 \\times 5) \\times (2^2 \\times 3)\\]\nCombining the powers of 2, we get:\n\\[2^1 \\times 2^2 \\times 2^1 \\times 2^3 \\times 2^1 \\times 2^2 = 2^{1+2+1+3+1+2} = 2^{10}\\]\nAnd combining the powers of 3 and 5, we get:\n\\[3^1 \\times 3^1 = 3^2\\]\n\\[5^1 = 5^1\\]\nSo the prime factorization of the product is:\n\\[2^{10} \\times 3^2 \\times 5^1\\]\n\n","prefix_end":783,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,1246,1657,4727,31340,525,9363,315,17767,17,1124,15136,220,19,1124,15136,220,21,1124,15136,220,23,1124,15136,220,16,15,1124,15136,220,16,17,59,701,582,1191,553,9271,279,10250,8168,2022,315,279,1985,382,5338,11,582,8168,551,1817,315,279,5109,510,78045,17,284,220,17,59,921,78045,19,284,220,17,61,17,59,921,78045,21,284,220,17,1124,15136,220,18,59,921,78045,23,284,220,17,61,18,59,921,78045,16,15,284,220,17,1124,15136,220,20,59,921,78045,16,17,284,220,17,61,17,1124,15136,220,18,59,2533,7039,11,582,30270,1493,8168,8040,3786,510,78045,17,1124,15136,220,19,1124,15136,220,21,1124,15136,220,23,1124,15136,220,16,15,1124,15136,220,16,17,284,220,17,1124,15136,220,17,61,17,1124,15136,320,17,1124,15136,220,18,8,1124,15136,220,17,61,18,1124,15136,320,17,1124,15136,220,20,8,1124,15136,320,17,61,17,1124,15136,220,18,10699,921,36192,5740,279,13430,315,220,17,11,582,633,510,78045,17,61,16,1124,15136,220,17,61,17,1124,15136,220,17,